            <ArticleTitle>Study of middle infrared difference frequency generation using a femtosecond laser source in LGT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3698-3701</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1364/OL.42.003698</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We demonstrate phase-matched difference frequency generation in the emerging nonlinear crystal La3Ga5.5Ta0.5O14. Tunable wavelengths between 1.4 and 4.7 μm are generated by using femtosecond sources. We also report on the measurements of the optical damage threshold in the femtosecond regime and on the nonlinear refractive index n2.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
